# Copy this to .env only if you need to override defaults. The lab
# runs cleanly with none of these set — setup.py has sensible
# defaults for every one.
#
# =========================================================================
# WHAT THIS LAB IS NOT
# =========================================================================
# This lab pins the fully-local claude-context path (Milvus + Ollama).
# It DELIBERATELY does not exercise the quickstart-default hosted path
# (Zilliz Cloud + OpenAI). If any of the variables below are set, setup.py
# refuses to proceed:
#
#   OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENAI_BASE_URL (when pointed off-loopback)
#   VOYAGEAI_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#   ZILLIZ_URI, ZILLIZ_CLOUD_URI
#   ZILLIZ_TOKEN, ZILLIZ_CLOUD_TOKEN
#
# The lab has to be reproducible without a paid account, and the whole
# point of the `no_default_egress` probe is that neither the CLI nor
# the MCP server should be reaching for these on the local path. If you
# genuinely need to test the hosted path, do so in a separate branch
# with its own results file — do not mix arms.
# =========================================================================

# --- Fixture selection --------------------------------------------------
# Absolute path to the fixture you want to index. Not required for
# --check; required for --install-fixture and --index. Point this at
# a directory that already exists on your machine.
#
# CLAUDE_CONTEXT_FIXTURE=/absolute/path/to/gratibot

# --- Lab state location -------------------------------------------------
# Where setup.py writes cached artifacts, summaries, and status. The
# default is $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ai-code-intelligence/claude-context/
# (~/.cache/ai-code-intelligence/claude-context on Linux, and
# ~/Library/Caches/ai-code-intelligence/claude-context on macOS).
# Overriding is useful for CI or when you want a per-branch state dir.
#
# CLAUDE_CONTEXT_LAB_STATE=/absolute/path/to/state

# --- Milvus bind ---------------------------------------------------------
# Loopback is the default. The lab does not test LAN-exposed Milvus;
# if you want to see what shared_dev_instance looks like across
# processes on the same machine, leave this at 127.0.0.1.
#
# MILVUS_HOST=127.0.0.1
# MILVUS_GRPC_PORT=19530

# --- Ollama bind ---------------------------------------------------------
# Also loopback by default. If you point at a remote Ollama, the lab's
# no_default_egress probe will (correctly) fire — do not do that on the
# `no_default_egress` measurement runs.
#
# OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11434
# OLLAMA_EMBEDDING_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
